/android/app/release

# Signing material — never commit these to a public repository.
# Matched at any depth on purpose: the release keystore is kept inside the
# working tree, so a rule anchored to one directory would not protect it after
# a move. A leaked key cannot be rotated without breaking in-place updates for
# every existing install, so `.githooks/pre-commit` blocks these as well, since
# .gitignore alone does not stop `git add -f`.
**/key.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pepk
# iOS/macOS signing, for when those ship
*.p8
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
